## A Complete config.json Example

Here's what a config.json looks like with both a cloud model and a local model configured:

```json
{
  "models": [
    {
      "title": "Claude Sonnet (Cloud)",
      "provider": "anthropic",
      "model": "claude-sonnet-4-6",
      "apiKey": "sk-ant-your-key"
    },
    {
      "title": "Local Phi-4 (Ollama)",
      "provider": "ollama",
      "model": "phi4"
    }
  ],
  "tabAutocompleteModel": {
    "title": "Tab Autocomplete (Ollama)",
    "provider": "ollama",
    "model": "phi4"
  }
}
```

With this config, you can switch between Claude and your local model using the model picker at the top of the Continue sidebar. You might use Claude for complex refactors and the local model for quick questions about private code.
